From 282e2cdcec74d51e9b91b09711a2f7552a4042ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:24:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] sfc_sice ice3lay: do not divide the excess heat by delt
 again

The excess lower-layer heat h2*ci*(T2-tfi) is in J/m2, but ice3lay converts
it to an ice thickness change with li*delt, deleting (1 - 1/delt) of it
while T2 is still reset.

Divide by li only.

Not triggered in the March test case (thin ice near melting).

Part of a water-conservation project for UFS physics (NOAA GML / CIRES).

AI-assisted: written with Claude Opus 5.5; reviewed by author
---
 physics/SFC_Models/SeaIce/CICE/sfc_sice.f | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/physics/SFC_Models/SeaIce/CICE/sfc_sice.f b/physics/SFC_Models/SeaIce/CICE/sfc_sice.f
index 3d7ecd2d..d4bc5df6 100644
--- a/physics/SFC_Models/SeaIce/CICE/sfc_sice.f
+++ b/physics/SFC_Models/SeaIce/CICE/sfc_sice.f
@@ -727,7 +727,7 @@
      &                    + (one - f1)*stsice(i,2)
 
               if (stsice(i,2) > tfi) then
-                hice(i) = hice(i) - h2*ci*(stsice(i,2) - tfi)/ (li*delt)
+                hice(i) = hice(i) - h2*ci*(stsice(i,2) - tfi)/ li
                 stsice(i,2) = tfi
               endif
             else
